to-paul-chiusano-source : List Word
to-paul-chiusano-source = lines-of (cons "# Paul Chiusano"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Paul, this page is about what hyperactivity takes from Unison and what it gives back. Every part of your work that hyperactivity builds on is yours, with full credit. Its paper names Unison as the precedent for content-addressed definitions"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p2 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ", and Avik has carried it for years as central to his thinking on interaction and languages"
  (cons (cite metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-source "(Part III, Unison)")
  (cons ". His name for what he wants to build with you is Unison + Univalence."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What you saw that the field still hasn't"
  (cons ""
  (cons "The field reads Unison as a nice idea for build caching. That misses what you did. You took naming out of the identity of code. A definition is its contents; a name is a label attached to a hash and changeable at no cost; the codebase is a database of definitions, not a pile of text files a compiler re-reads. Unison 1.0 shows what follows: nothing is compiled twice, renaming never breaks anything, most version conflicts never arise, and one typed program can deploy itself across machines, because shipping code means shipping hashes and the receiver fetches only what it lacks."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Your 2024 post on where Unison is headed makes the same point from the systems side: distributed systems stop being tedious once serialization, networking and deployment are not hand-written boilerplate. Abilities complete the picture: effects are typed and handled, so the same code runs against a local handler or a cloud one. You started from *Functional Programming in Scala* with Rúnar and went where most functional programmers have not followed: code is not text, and identity is not a name."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What hyperactivity takes up"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Hyperactivity is in Avik's words a language and “a computational model of reality i.e. wolfram's ruliad executing on silicon”, with cubical type theory at its core"
  (cons (cite s1-1-p4 "(§1.1)")
  (cons ". In its content-addressed codebase a definition is stored with its typed syntax tree and dependency references; a name is a view or alias; a stable reference identifies a definition, so renaming does not change what dependents refer to"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p2 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ". The codebase holds not only programs but their typing derivations, semantics, equivalences, transformations, dependency certificates and reusable proofs"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p6 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ". In hyperactivity the hash is the reference, and the names log records who pointed which name at which content, and when"
  (cons (cite metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-source "(Part III, Unison)")
  (cons ". This page is itself such a definition, and each link on it opens the definition it cites."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What it closes: univalence"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Content addressing alone stops at one place, and you know it well. The paper separates three statements: two definitions have the same digest, they are definitionally equal, or a specified relation holds between their meanings"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p4 "(10.22)")
  (cons ". A digest identifies a representation and does not prove semantic equivalence"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p3 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ". When someone improves a definition, the new version is a new hash, and the reason the move preserves meaning has, until now, lived outside the codebase."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Univalence closes that. An equivalence becomes an identification, and transport along it computes"
  (cons (cite s1-1-p5 "(§1.1)")
  (cons "; operations and their laws are transported together across a structural equivalence"
  (cons (cite s4-p2 "(§4)")
  (cons ". The store records each relation between definitions with its actual evidence and uses the strongest available one for the operation being performed"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p5 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ", and an edit's effect on its dependents is computed by the same dependency operations used for persistent evaluation"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p6 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ". A refactor stops being two unrelated hashes: it is a relation with its evidence, kept in the store."
  (cons ""
  (cons "The same holds for abilities. A handler supplies an interpretation of requests in a particular world, and different handlers yield different observations of the same process description"
  (cons (cite s10-p6 "(§10)")
  (cons ". Specialization returns a new code together with a code for its justification"
  (cons (cite s6-2-p6 "(§6.2)")
  (cons ", and rewriting a residual by a theorem carries a path checked against the original"
  (cons (cite s6-2-p11 "(§6.2)")
  (cons ", so the fast version is connected to the general one by a checked relation. The design objective is zero marginal proof-writing beyond the reasoning already required"
  (cons (cite s1-p26 "(§1)")
  (cons ": your never compile twice becomes never prove twice."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Why this matters to Unison Cloud"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Unison Cloud sends a program to a network, which fetches its dependencies by hash. In the paper a peer sends a definition, its dependency closure and its proofs, and the recipient checks and uses them in its own context; a shared global namespace is unnecessary for definition identity"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p7 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ". Two protocol versions can coexist, their compatibility determined by their actual interpreters"
  (cons (cite s10-11-p7 "(§10.11)")
  (cons ". With relations between definitions kept with their evidence, caching and migration across nodes can go by meaning, not only by bytes."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## The offer"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Avik wants to work with you, not around you. Unison has the codebase model, the tooling, Unison Share, Unison Cloud, and a community that already thinks of code as content-addressed data. Hyperactivity has the type theory that makes equality between definitions part of the code. Your name is on the part of this that is yours, all of it, everywhere the work's lineage is told: beside Rúnar Bjarnason and Arya Irani, beside Arthur Brock and Eric Harris-Braun's Ceptr, Statebox, Voevodsky and the cubical type theory authors."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Sources"
  (cons ""
  (cons "- Unison 1.0 announcement, Unison Computing, November 2025, https://unison-lang.org/unison-1-0"
  (cons "- Where Unison is headed, Paul Chiusano, June 2024, https://www.unison-lang.org/blog/where-unison-is-headed/"
  (cons "- Unison roadmap, https://unison-lang.org/roadmap"
  (cons "- Unison 1.0 released, AlternativeTo, November 2025, https://alternativeto.net/news/2025/11/unison-1-0-released-with-stable-language-cloud-deployment-and-improved-tools"
  (cons "- Trying out Unison, part 4: from the edge to the cloud, SoftwareMill, https://softwaremill.com/trying-out-unison-part-4-from-the-edge-to-the-cloud"
  (cons "- Avik Jain, hyperactivity, Parts I and III, the definitions linked above"
  nil))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
